to  talk to servers rather than through a user interface.  It can
aid in troubleshooting, when it might be necessary to verify what
data a server is sending in response to commands  issued  by  the
client.   For example, to retrieve the home page of a web site: $
printf "GET / HTTP/1.0\r\n\r\n" |  nc  host.example.com  80  Note
that this also displays the headers sent by the web server.  They
can be filtered, using a tool such as if necessary.  More compli‐
